# Nova Pentacle (CR 602.3, 609.7a, 614.1a, 611.2a): the opponent may choose a creature of their own as the target ("it
# doesn't have to be a creature that opponent controls"), only the chosen source's damage to the activating player is
# redirected, and the effect lasts only the turn. On turn 3 Bot1 activates the Pentacle with exactly three sources, Bot2
# targets its own Sanctuary Cat (1/2), and Bot1 chooses that Cat as the source. Bot2's Lightning Bolt then deals 3 to Bot1:
# not from the chosen source, so it is dealt to Bot1 (17). Bot1's own Cat attacks and Bot2's Cat blocks: the chosen source's
# damage to Bot1's Cat is not damage to Bot1, so each Cat takes 1, and the effect still waits. On turn 4 Bot2's Cat attacks:
# the effect ended with turn 3, so its 1 damage is dealt to Bot1 (16) and not to the Cat.

